### Food Delivery Platform - Chat Service (support chat)
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
###
### Every customer, restaurant owner and delivery partner has at most ONE conversation, with Support.
### All platform admins share one inbox and any of them can read and answer. There is no conversation id on the
### participant side: the API always works on the caller's own conversation. Plain text only.
### New messages are announced on the live WebSocket (notification-service); the page then re-reads over REST.
###
### Caller identity: the access token's role, CUSTOMER (or RESTAURANT_ADMIN / DELIVERY_PARTNER) for /chat,
### PLATFORM_ADMIN for /admin/chat. clientMessageId is a UUID the client invents once per message: sending the
### same one again returns the saved message (200) instead of a duplicate. {{$guid}} makes a new one per request,
### so to try the retry, copy the id of a request into a fixed value.

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@service = http://localhost:8096
@customerEmail = meera.iyer@example.com
@customerPassword = Meera1234
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123
@customerId = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.userId}}
# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@conversationId = {{customerSends.response.body.$.conversationId}}
@retryId = 6f1c3a52-0f4b-4d52-9e56-3d6d3f0f0a11


### ============================ CUSTOMER ============================

### 1. Customer login -> customerId
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{customerEmail}}", "password": "{{customerPassword}}" }

### 2. My conversation (404 until I wrote the first message: the UI shows an empty chat)
GET {{service}}/api/v1/chat/conversation
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 3. Write to Support (201; creates the conversation on the first message)
###    body: 1 to 2000 characters after trimming; 429 above 30 messages a minute; 503 when user-service is down.
# @name customerSends
POST {{service}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Where is my order?", "clientMessageId": "{{$guid}}" }

### 4. The same message again (a retry after a lost response) -> 200 with the same message, nothing duplicated
POST {{service}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Retry of the same message", "clientMessageId": "{{retryId}}" }

### 5. My messages: the latest 30, oldest first. hasMore / nextBeforeId page backwards:
###    GET .../messages?beforeId=<nextBeforeId>&limit=30
GET {{service}}/api/v1/chat/messages?limit=30
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 6. I read Support's messages (204; Support sees the ticks turn double)
POST {{service}}/api/v1/chat/read
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 7. A blank message -> 400
POST {{service}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "   ", "clientMessageId": "{{$guid}}" }

### 8. Platform admins have no conversation of their own -> 403
GET {{service}}/api/v1/chat/conversation
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ============================ ADMIN (the shared inbox) ============================

### 9. Admin login -> adminToken
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

### 10. The inbox: my pinned first, then the latest activity. search: name or last message; size at most 50.
###     participant.online is null when presence is unknown.
GET {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations?search=&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 11. How many conversations wait for an answer (the menu badge)
GET {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 12. One conversation
GET {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 13. Its messages (same paging); q searches the text inside this conversation (case-insensitive)
GET {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?limit=30&q=order
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 14. I read it (204). The inbox is shared: this clears the unread count for every admin.
POST {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 15. Answer as Support (201); signed with my name from user-service ("Support" if it cannot tell)
POST {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "It left the kitchen five minutes ago.", "clientMessageId": "{{$guid}}" }

### 16. Pin and mute are mine only (200 with the conversation)
PUT {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/pin
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pinned": true }

###
PUT {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/mute
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "muted": true }

### 17. Start (or open) the conversation with a user: 201 when new, 200 when it existed.
###     404 unknown user, 422 for a platform admin.
POST {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{customerId}} }

### 18. Customers cannot read the admin API -> 403
GET {{service}}/api/v1/admin/chat/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
